        "reason": "The evidence supports an answer. The abstract states Twitter data makes better predictions about the language inventory per country. In the Discussion, the authors provide an explanation/hypothesis: Twitter data matches populations better when weighted by GDP and worse by internet usage, implying Twitter represents wealthier populations, or that their collection is urban-centered. The Discussion also states Twitter has fewer missing languages than web data. So a hypothesis is indeed offered (wealthier/urban populations producing more Twitter coverage, hence fewer missed languages)."
